Expression, Challenge, Relation, Change, Meaning, Role, and Collective;
and wherein a transition probability $P(a \Rightarrow b)$ between
reasoning layers $a$ and $b$ is adjusted as:

$$P(a \Rightarrow b) = \frac{P_{0}(a \Rightarrow b)\,\kappa(\text{anchor},a,b)}{Z}.$$

where $P_{0}(a \Rightarrow b)$ is a baseline transition probability,
$\kappa(\text{anchor},a,b)$ is an anchor weighting function applied to
the transition, and $Z$ is a normalization constant; it being understood
that other equivalent formulations of anchor-based modulation may also
be employed, including additive offsets, non-linear scaling functions,
or probabilistic mixtures of multiple anchors.

\[19\] The method of claim \[18\], further comprising dynamically
