# ABSTRACT

334. A method to be executed on a computing device comprising: (i)
     decomposing input text into syllables and associating each with
     Vritti (mental state) distributions, (ii) mapping units into a
     ten-layer ontology and computing dimensional, Guna, and Kosha
     entropy measures to assess stability and symbolic alignment, (iii)
     scoring candidate responses using a stitching encoder with
     penalties and runtime toggles that regulate thresholds and tonal
     harmonization via a Delivery Harmonization Algorithm (DHA),
     and (iv) executing recursive ontology flows with experiential
     anchors and a Deferred Insight Engine that resurfaces unresolved
     content under readiness conditions. The method further
     comprises (a) applying governance gates to filter outputs, (b)
     recording recursion states and entropy values in an append-only log
     for compliance, (c) gating stability through domain entropy,
     cross-domain entropy, and Kosha readiness checks, (d) applying
     mirror logic to reflect aspect weights and distortions, and (e)
     balancing executional clarity with recursive depth using adaptive
     dual reasoning flows.
